.nh
.TH "PB-SSH" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-ssh - Connect to a machine with OpenSSH


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb ssh [user@]<machine> [-- <OpenSSH arguments...>] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Connect to a machine with OpenSSH

.PP
Connect to an enrolled machine through OpenSSH using Paperboat resolution. Optional arguments after -- go to OpenSSH; the command preserves SSH host-key verification and reports identity changes for deliberate approval.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for ssh

.PP
\fB--user\fP=""
	remote operating-system user


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-ssh-doctor(1)\fP, \fBpb-ssh-trust-host(1)\fP
